---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
        title="About Sim"
        description="The open-source workspace for building and deploying AI agent workflows."
        pubDate={new Date('February 24 2025')}
        heroImage="/blog-placeholder-about.jpg"
>
        <p>
                Sim is built by Sim Studio to make AI automation approachable. Instead of wrangling sprawling codebases,
                you stitch together agents, tools, and blocks on a visual canvas and run them immediately. It is the
                fastest way to design, debug, and deploy agentic systems for customer support, data enrichment, and
                internal operations.
        </p>

        <p>
                Our Copilot sits alongside you in the builder, generating new nodes, fixing errors, and iterating on flows
                with plain language. When you need trustworthy answers, you can upload documents to a vector database so
                agents stay grounded in your own content rather than hallucinating.
        </p>

        <p>
                You can start instantly in the cloud at <a href="https://sim.ai" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">sim.ai</a>
                or self-host with Docker. Choose between quick npm scaffolding (<code>npx simstudio</code>), a production-ready
                Docker Compose stack, or an Ollama-powered profile for local models. vLLM endpoints with OpenAI-compatible
                APIs are supported too, so your deployment can match your security and latency needs.
        </p>

        <p>
                We love hearing what you are building. Join the Sim community on
                <a href="https://discord.gg/Hr4UWYEcTT" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Discord</a> or browse the
                <a href="https://github.com/simstudioai/sim" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">open-source repository</a>
                to contribute.
        </p>
</Layout>
